<title>GERMANY: None should doubt EMU determination - De Charette.</title>
<headline>None should doubt EMU determination - De Charette.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Foreign Minister Herve de Charette said on Monday that no one should doubt the determination of France and Germany to stick to their plans for European monetary union (EMU).</p>
<p>&quot;You must not doubt the determination of both governments to apply what we have decided,&quot; de Charette said at a joint news conference after meeting his German counterpart Klaus Kinkel.</p>
<p>When the decision is made on the initial EMU participants in early 1998, france and Germany will have met the criteria and they will be ready to start the currency union on schedule in 1999, he said.</p>
</text>
